{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790307220,"nonce":"6jPSgzD/aPBynsVUIVFla0TPyOY=","title":"Cranelift frames larger than a page skip the Windows stack guard page","message":"host_isa leaves `enable_probestack` at its default, false. A Windows thread's stack is reserved and committed a page at a time as the guard page below the committed part is touched; a prologue that moves the stack pointer more than a page and then touches memory lands past the guard page, in reserved but uncommitted memory, and faults with an access violation instead of growing the stack. Rust and LLVM emit __chkstk for such frames; Cranelift emits probes only when asked.\n\nFix: on Windows set `enable_probestack=true` with `probestack_strategy=inline` (no probestack symbol to link). Unix is unchanged. Found by reading while looking for the cause of cd215b0; not observed in a log.","files":null}]}